From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: add the DisplayPort audio link

Enabling the DisplayPort controller gave the handset video over the Type-C
dock but no sound through it. The controller registers an hdmi-audio-codec
and already carries #sound-dai-cells, and the DSP side already knows the
DISPLAY_PORT_RX port, but the sound card never referenced either, so no PCM
and no sink existed for the external display.

Add the missing back end.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -421,6 +421,22 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	dp-dai-link {
+		link-name = "DisplayPort Playback";
+
+		cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&q6afedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX>;
+		};
+
+		platform {
+			sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+		};
+
+		codec {
+			sound-dai = <&mdss_dp>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	speaker-dai-link {
 		link-name = "Speaker Playback";
 
--
2.50.1
